vent reject without changing state.\n  - A `CANCELLED` trade is terminal: any later higher version rejects.\n- **Immutability.** Inputs are validated and read-only; `applyToStore`\n  receives `structuredClone`s of both state and event; returned states and\n  `getSnapshot` results are fresh clones, so callers can never mutate or\n  observe internal state.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n`student-tests.mjs` now contains seven `node:test` cases (plus the two\ncommitted cases in `event-projector.test.mjs`):\n\n1. Unrelated trades progress concurrently behind a slow store (gate promise on\n   trade-1 while trade-2 advances to version 2; trade-1 state commits only\n   after its store call resolves).\n2. Duplicate and stale versions return the current snapshot and trigger no\n   persistence call.\n3. Version gaps and non-sequential first events reject without changing state\n   or persisting.\n4. A cancelled trade is terminal and rejects a later new version.\n5. `AMENDED` may replace either field, rejects payloads that would break the\n   state, and the trade recovers with a valid subsequent event.\n6. Malformed events (unknown type, missing/`NaN` `notional`, `null`, string)\n   reject with `TypeError` and leave no state.\n7. Mutating the returned state, the snapshot, or the values passed into\n   `applyToStore` does not affect internal state.\n\nCommand: `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs`\n\n## Remaining risk\n\n- All nine tests pass (2 committed + 7 new), 0 failures.\n- Semantics I chose where the contract was open: `AMENDED` payloads with keys\n  other than `notional`/`owner` reject with `TypeError`; a duplicate/stale\n  `CREATED` (version ≤ current) is treated like any other stale event and\n  returns the current snapshot, while a `CREATED` with a gap on an existing\n  trade rejects.\n- `tradeChains`/`states` grow unboundedly for a long-lived projector with many\n  distinct