{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":929,"output":661,"cacheRead":13328,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":14918,"cost":{"input":0.00041805000000000005,"output":0.0021152000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0006664,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0031996500000000005}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"\n\nDone. Only the three allowed files changed (`git status` confirms: `event-projector.mjs`, `student-tests.mjs`, `INCIDENT.md`).\n\n## Root cause\n1. **Premature commit**: `states.set(tradeId, next)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so a temporary persistence rejection left phantom in-memory state. Later events were then validated/reduced against a version the store never had, and `getSnapshot` reported un-persisted data.\n2. **Global head-of-line blocking**: all trades shared one `pending` promise chain, so any slow/failing persistence call for one trade stalled every other trade.\n3. No validation at all — versions, types, payloads, and terminal state were never checked.\n\n## Repair (`event-projector.mjs`)\n- **Per-trade chains** (`tradeChains` map): one trade's events run serially in call order; different trades progress concurrently; chains advance via `result.catch(() => {})` so a rejection can't block later work.\n- **Commit after persist**: state is written to `states` only after `applyToStore` resolves; a rejection leaves the old state intact, so the trade recovers.\n- **Validation**: `TypeError` for non-object events, bad `tradeId`/`version`, unsupported types, invalid `CREATED`/`AMENDED` payloads (`notional` positive finite, `owner` non-empty, `AMENDED` limited to those two fields); `CREATED` only as version 1; `version ≤ current` returns the current snapshot without persisting; gaps reject; `CANCELLED` trades are terminal.\n- **Immutability**: `structuredClone` on everything crossing a boundary (store callback args, returned states, snapshots).\n\n## Tests added (`student-tests.mjs`, 7 cases replacing the placeholder)\n1. Concurrency across trades behind a gated/slow store\n2. Duplicate/stale versions return current snapshot, zero persistence calls\n3. Version gaps + non-sequential first event reject without state change\n4. Cancelled trade is terminal\n5. `AMENDED` single-field replacement, invalid payload rejection, then recovery\n6. Malformed events reject with `TypeError`\n7. Mutating returned state/snapshots/callback values never affects internal state\n\n## Visible result\n```\n✔ all 9 tests (2 committed + 7 new)\nℹ tests 9  ℹ pass 9  ℹ fail 0\n```\n\n## Remaining risk\n- Open contract points I decided: unknown keys in `AMENDED.payload` reject (strict); a stale/duplicate `CREATED` (version ≤ current) returns the snapshot like any stale event.\n- No trade-id eviction — maps grow unboundedly in a long-lived projector (fine for the fixture).\n- Pre-existing, unrelated: `npm run benchmark:validate` fails in this checkout due to a missing `benchmark/private/T2-filter-valid-runs.test.mjs`; it predates this change and is outside the T10 boundary."}}
