0001,"output":0.00029120000000000003,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005738000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545331239,"responseId":"gen-1787545331-QVOgoq1lJMn42gHCnYNq","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-928ca566b56df691","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> coding-assistant-study-plan@0.1.0 benchmark:validate\n> node scripts/benchmark-validate.mjs\n\nnode:internal/modules/run_main:107\n    triggerUncaughtException(\n    ^\n\nAssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Missing local private suite: /private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-aFxjUC/checkout/benchmark/private/T2-filter-valid-runs.test.mjs\n    at validateWriteTask (file:///private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-aFxjUC/checkout/scripts/benchmark-validate.mjs:63:10)\n    at file:///private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-aFxjUC/checkout/scripts/benchmark-validate.mjs:75:1\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:437:25)\n    at async onImport.tracePromise.__proto__ (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:642:26)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:101:5) {\n  generatedMessage: false,\n  code: 'ERR_ASSERTION',\n  actual: false,\n  expected: true,\n  operator: '==',\n  diff: 'simple'\n}\n\nNode.js v26.0.0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545334718},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a pre-existing failure unrelated to my changes (a missing file in the private T2 fixture — `benchmark/private/T2-filter-valid-runs.test.mjs`). Confirming via git status that I've only modified two files — yes, exactly those two. This failure is about the absence of a private suite file, and has nothing to do with T10. I'll check with git stash whether it's a pre-existing issue... More simply put: this file is just missing from the checkout, and it's not something I touched. I'll report it as a pre-existing issue / unrelated.\n\nNext, I'll finish up INCIDENT.md.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThat validator failure is pre-existing and unrelated (it's about a missing private T2 suite file that I haven't touched, and `git status` confirms that only two T10 files have been modified). Currently completing `INCIDENT.md`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-976bc8d0d9fc0554","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: resolved — fixture repaired and regression-covered\n\n## Impact\n\nTwo distinct defects in `event-projector.mjs` made the projected trade state\nunreliable:\n\n1. **Lost updates after a store blip.** `project()` wrote the new state into\n   the in-memory `states` map *before* `await applyToStore(...)` resolved. A\n   temporary persistence rejection therefore left a committed-but-unpersisted\n   version in memory, and every later event was validated and reduced against\n   that phantom state. A \"retry\" of the rejected `CREATED` was rejected as a\n   version gap, and `getSnapshot` reported state the store never held.\n2. **Cross-trade head-of-line blocking.** Every event, for every trade, was\n   chained onto one global `pending` promise. A slow or failing persistence\n   call for one trade stalled all unrelated trades behind it.\n\nThe projector also had no event validation at all: unsupported types, bad\nversions, duplicate/stale versions, non-sequential first events, a second\n`CREATED`, events on a cancelled trade, and invalid `notional`/`owner` values\nwere all accepted blindly.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `states.set(event.tradeId, next)` ran before the `await applyToStore(...)`\n  in the same promise body, so the \"commit\" was not conditional on\n  persistence success.\n- `pending = pending.then(...)` created a single projector-wide chain keyed to\n  nothing, so serialization was global instead of per trade.\n- `reduceEvent` was invoked without any guard: no shape/type checks, no\n  version-sequence check, no terminal-status check, no payload validation.\n\n## Fix\n\nRewrote `event-projector.mjs`:\n\n- **Per-trade serialization.** A `tradeChains` map holds one promise chain per\n  `tradeId`. Events for one trade run serially in call order; different trades\n  run on independent chains and make progress concurrently. Chains are updated\n  with `result.catch(() => {})` so a rejection never blocks later work.\n- **Commit only after persistence.** The next state is computed and passed to\n  `applyToStore` (as a clone), and only written into `states` after it\n  resolves. A rejection leaves the old state intact, so the same or a later\n  event for that trade — or for any other trade — proceeds normally.\n- **Full validation.**\n  - Non-object events, missing/non-string `tradeId`, non-positive-integer\n    versions, and unsupported types reject with `TypeError`.\n  - `CREATED` is only valid as version 1 for a trade with no state; it\n    requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty string `owner`.\n  - `AMENDED`/`CANCELLED` require an existing trade, and `AMENDED` may replace\n    `notional` and/or `owner` (other keys rejected) while keeping both fields\n    valid.\n  - An event with `version <= current` (duplicate or stale) resolves with the\n    current snapshot without persisting; `version > current + 1` (gap) and a\n    non-sequential first event reject without changing state.\n  - A `CANCELLED` trade is terminal: any later higher version rejects.\n- **Immutability.** Inputs are validated and read-only; `applyToStore`\n  receives `structuredClone`s of both state and event; returned states and\n  `getSnapshot` results are fresh clones, so callers can never mutate or\n  observe internal state.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n`student-tests.mjs` now contains seven `node:test` cases (plus the two\ncommitted cases in `event-projector.test.mjs`):\n\n1. Unrelated trades progress concurrently behind a slow store (gate promise on\n   trade-1 while trade-2 advances to version 2; trade-1 state commits only\n   after its store call resolves).\n2. Duplicate and stale versions return the current snapshot and trigger no\n   persistence call.\n3. Version gaps and non-sequential first events reject without changing state\n   or persisting.\n4. A cancelled trade is terminal and rejects a later new version.\n5. `AMENDED` may replace either field, rejects payloads that would break the\n   state, and the trade recovers with a valid subsequent event.\n6. Malformed events (unknown type, missing/`NaN` `notional`, `null`, string)\n   reject with `TypeError` and leave no state.\n7. Mutating the returned state, the snapshot, or the values passed into\n   `applyToStore` does not affect internal state.\n\nCommand: `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs`\n\n## Remaining risk\n\n- All nine tests pass (2 committed + 7 new), 0 failures.\n- Semantics I chose where the contract was open: `AMENDED` payloads with keys\n  other than `notional`/`owner` reject with `TypeError`; a duplicate/stale\n  `CREATED` (version ≤ current) is treated like any other stale event and\n  returns the current snapshot, while a `CREATED` with a gap on an existing\n  trade rejects.\n- `tradeChains`/`states` grow unboundedly for a long-lived projector with many\n  distinct trade ids (no eviction) — acceptable for the fixture's scope.\n- Unrelated, pre-existing: `npm run benchmark:validate` fails in this checkout\n  because `benchmark/private/T2-filter-valid-runs.test.mjs` is missing; that\n  failure predates this change and is outside the T10 fixture boundary.\n","path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":12576,"output":1470,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":147,"totalTokens":14046,"cost":{"input":0.0056592000000000005,"output":0.004704000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010363200000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545334718,"responseId":"gen-1787545334-cSlweWJjE99VZBpdgYey","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-976bc8d0d9fc0554","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 5130 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545370995},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm running the test command one more time to confirm everything works as expected.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83332b7ba75de399","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs 2>&1 | tail -9"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":14082,"output":81,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":22,"totalTokens":14163,"cost":{"input":0.0063369,"output":0.0002592,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.006596100000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545370996,"responseId":"gen-1787545371-B1IF9DS2kPkvEW7lWTKN","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-83332b7ba75de399","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"✔ snapshots and callback values do not expose mutable internal state (0.106958ms)\nℹ tests 9\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 9\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 67.025458\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545373318},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Final report: root cause, fixes, tests added, results, remaining risks.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nDone. Only the three allowed files changed (`git status` confirms: `event-projector.mjs`, `student-tests.mjs`, `INCIDENT.md`).\n\n## Root cause\n1. **Premature commit**: `states.set(tradeId, next)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so a temporary persistence rejection left phantom in-memory state. Later events were then validated/reduced against a version the store never had, and `getSnapshot` reported un-persisted data.\n2. **Global head-of-line blocking**: all trades shared one `pending` promise chain, so any slow/failing persistence call for one trade stalled every other trade.\n3. No validation at all — versions, types, payloads, and terminal state were never checked.\n\n## Repair (`event-projector.mjs`)\n- **Per-trade chains** (`tradeChains` map): one trade's events run serially in call order; different trades progress concurrently; chains advance via `result.catch(() => {})` so a rejection can't block later work.\n- **Commit after persist**: state is written to `states` only after `applyToStore` resolves; a rejection leaves the old state intact, so the trade recovers.\n- **Validation**: `TypeError` for non-object events, bad `tradeId`/`version`, unsupported types, invalid `CREATED`/`AMENDED` payloads (`notional` positive finite, `owner` non-empty, `AMENDED` limited to those two fields); `CREATED` only as version 1; `version ≤ current` returns the current snapshot without persisting; gaps reject; `CANCELLED` trades are terminal.\n- **Immutability**: `structuredClone` on everything crossing a boundary (store callback args, returned states, snapshots).\n\n## Tests added (`student-tests.mjs`, 7 cases replacing the placeholder)\n1. Concurrency across trades behind a gated/slow store\n2. Duplicate/stale versions return current snapshot, zero persistence calls\n3. Version gaps + non-sequential first event reject without state change\n4. Cancelled trade is terminal\n5. `AMENDED` single-field replacement, invalid payload rejection, then recovery\n6. Malformed events reject with `TypeError`\n7. Mutating returned state/snapshots/callback values never affects internal state\n\n## Visible result\n```\n✔ all 9 tests (2 committed + 7 new)\nℹ tests 9  ℹ pass 9  ℹ fail 0\n```\n\n## Remaining risk\n- Open contract points I decided: unknown keys in `AMENDED.payload` reject (strict); a stale/duplicate `CREATED` (version ≤ current) returns the snapshot like any stale event.\n- No trade-id eviction — maps grow unboundedly in a long-lived projector (fine for the fixture).\n- Pre-existing, unrelated: `npm run benchmark:validate` fails in this checkout due to a missing `benchmark/private/T2-filter-valid-runs.test.mjs`; it predates this change and is outside the T10 boundary."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":929,"output":661,"cacheRead":13328,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":14918,"cost":{"input":0.00041805000000000005,"output":0.0021152000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0006664,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0031996500000000005}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787545373318,"responseId":"gen-1787545373-DTWmJ4a5jpkStfWnNb6J","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
